# The Moon's Scars

Long ago, when the world was young, the Moon was perfectly smooth and bright, the most beautiful jewel in the night sky. She was vain and proud, gazing at her reflection in every lake and ocean, believing herself superior to all celestial beings.

The Sun, her older brother, warned her: "Beauty without kindness means nothing." But Moon only laughed and turned away.

One night, a small star came seeking help. "Please, Moon, share some of your light. I'm too dim, and the travelers below cannot find their way."

"Find your own light," Moon replied coldly. "I will not diminish my beauty for anyone."

The star wept silver tears that fell to earth. The Sky Father heard this and grew angry. "If you will not share your blessings, then wear the marks of your pride forever."

He threw stones that struck the Moon's perfect face, leaving deep craters and shadows. No matter how Moon wept and apologized, the scars remained.

Now Moon lights the darkness faithfully, her pocked face a reminder to all: true beauty lies not in perfection, but in helping others. And on the darkest nights, when Moon hides her scarred face, she remembers the star she turned away.

